From: ios-veux
Subject: [PATCH] Use device I/O mapping for VEUX pmsg

The phone's pmsg dump after the ordered-write change still contains corrupted
XNU bytes. Use the conservative I/O memory mapping for the reserved pmsg RAM
instead of write-combining, while retaining the store barriers from patch 0094.
Give this logger a distinct start marker so the next dump identifies this build.

--- a/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
+++ b/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
@@ -758,5 +758,6 @@ veux_pmsg_init(void)
 	paddr = (vm_offset_t)(reg[0] + reg[1] - *pmsg_size);
-	vaddr = ml_io_map_wcomb(paddr, *pmsg_size);
+	/* Treat reserved persistent RAM as device I/O on the phone. */
+	vaddr = ml_io_map(paddr, *pmsg_size);
 	if (vaddr == 0) {
 		return false;
 	}
@@ -778,4 +778,4 @@ veux_pmsg_init(void)
-	static const char start[] = "\n--- XNU VEUX ramoops log start ---\n";
+	static const char start[] = "\n--- XNU VEUX pmsg device-map v2 ---\n";
 	for (unsigned int i = 0; i < sizeof(start) - 1; i++) {
 		veux_pmsg_putc(start[i]);
 	}
